# Lowercase identifiers in annotation position are now accepted as positional PropertyDict entries.
# Previously the parser required uppercase-headed identifiers in implied-call annotation position
# (e.g. `fn@[Int Null]`). The fix removes the uppercase guard so `fn@[a Null]` and `fn@[a b]`
# work as union type annotations with TypeVar members.
# This tests: fn@[a b] where both a and b are lowercase TypeVars is now a valid annotation.
[f: [fn@[a b] [x] x]]
=== out
["f": [fn@[a  b] [x] x]]
